-- CK-47: Elm's `exposing (T(..))` is one mistake and gets ONE diagnostic,
-- at the `(..)`, saying how beni exposes constructors (by name, beside the
-- type); the uses of `Decoding` and `Encoding` below then stay quiet, per
-- Elm's stop-at-first-phase rule. On 7427828 it is EXPECTED TOKEN, two
-- INVALID CHARACTERs on the same line, and one UNKNOWN CONSTRUCTOR per use.
--
-- The code and position are D8 as amended (checker-v2.md §21): `expected_token`
-- at the `(` after the type name, and the message suggests the n-ary form
-- `exposing (Direction, Decoding, Encoding)` — so it names the constructors.
import Schema exposing (Direction(..))


flip : Direction -> Direction
flip d =
    case d of
        Decoding ->
            Encoding

        Encoding ->
            Decoding
